  "parameters": [
    {
      "name": "NMDA_fraction_recurrent",
      "role": "Fraction of recurrent excitatory current via slow NMDA receptors \u2014 stabilizes bump.",
      "value": "~0.8"
    },
    {
      "name": "ring_size_N_E",
      "role": "Number of tuned excitatory neurons on the ring.",
      "value": "1024"
    },
    {
      "name": "N_I",
      "role": "Number of inhibitory interneurons.",
      "value": "256"
    },
    {
      "name": "excitatory_footprint_sigma",
      "role": "Width of like-to-like recurrent excitation on the ring.",
      "value": "~18\u00b0"
    },
    {
      "name": "delay_duration",
      "role": "Mnemonic delay over which the bump must persist.",
      "value": "~3-6 s"
    }
  ],
  "notes": "Ring attractor is discretized into 4 tuned pyramidal pools (0/90/180/270\u00b0) for tractability; in the full model this is a continuous ring of ~1024 neurons. PV+ inhibition is modeled as a single broad pool to capture unstructured feedback inhibition. SST and CB/CR interneurons are included to reflect interneuron diversity in dlPFC though the canonical 2000 model used a single I population. L5 pyramidal neurons serve as the readout layer for downstream projection."
}